# Code Quality Standards

## Java 25 LTS Best Practices

### Use Records for DTOs and Value Objects

```java
// Application layer DTOs
public record SearchContainersQuery(
    ExternalApiProvider backend,
    String containerNumber,
    TradeType tradeType
) implements Query<Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>>> {}

public record ContainerSearchResult(
    String containerNumber,
    String status,
    String terminalCode
) {}

// Web layer DTOs
public record ContainerSearchResponse(
    List<ContainerSearchResultItemResponse> results,
    int count
) {
    public static ContainerSearchResponse fromApplication(List<ContainerSearchResult> results) {
        return new ContainerSearchResponse(
            results.stream().map(ContainerSearchResultItemResponse::fromApplication).toList(),
            results.size()
        );
    }
}

// Infrastructure DTOs
public record EModalContainerFeeInventoryDto(
    String drayUnitId,
    String containerNumber,
    String status
) {}

// Domain value objects
public record Error(String code, String message) {
    public Error {
        if (code == null || code.isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Error code cannot be null or blank");
        }
    }
}
```

### Sealed Classes for Result Pattern

```java
public sealed interface Result<T> {
    record Success<T>(T value) implements Result<T> {}
    record Failure<T>(Error error) implements Result<T> {}
    
    static <T> Result<T> success(T value) { return new Success<>(value); }
    static <T> Result<T> failure(Error error) { return new Failure<>(error); }
    
    default <R> R match(Function<T, R> onSuccess, Function<Error, R> onFailure) {
        return switch (this) {
            case Success<T>(var value) -> onSuccess.apply(value);
            case Failure<T>(var error) -> onFailure.apply(error);
        };
    }
}
```

### Pattern Matching with Switch

```java
// Result pattern matching
var results = dispatcher.dispatch(query)
    .getOrThrow(error -> new DomainErrorException(error, mapErrorToHttpStatus(error)));

private HttpStatus mapErrorToHttpStatus(Error error) {
    return switch (error.code()) {
        case "Backend.Unsupported" -> HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST;
        case "Container.NotFound" -> HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND;
        case "Backend.ServiceUnavailable" -> HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE;
        default -> HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;
    };
}
```

### Text Blocks for Multi-line Strings

```java
@Operation(
    summary = "Search containers",
    description = """
        Searches for containers in the specified backend system.
        
        For eModal backend, this retrieves container fee inventory and LFD information.
        For CargoSprint backend, this retrieves basic container information.
        """
)
```

## Naming Conventions (Enforced by ArchUnit)

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Controller | `*Controller` with `@RestController` | `ContainerSearchController` |
| Query | `*Query` record implementing `Query<T>` | `SearchContainersQuery` |
| Command | `*Command` record implementing `Command<T>` | `RefreshTokenCommand` |
| Query Handler | `*QueryHandler` with `@Service` | `SearchContainersQueryHandler` |
| Command Handler | `*CommandHandler` with `@Service` | `ExchangeAuthCodeCommandHandler` |
| Result | `*Result` record | `ContainerSearchResult` |
| Port | `*Port` interface in `common/` | `KeycloakAuthPort` |
| Strategy | `*Strategy` interface | `ContainerSearchStrategy` |
| Web Request DTO | `*Request` record | `BulkContainerSearchRequest` |
| Web Response DTO | `*Response` record | `ContainerSearchResponse` |
| Infrastructure DTO | `*Dto` record | `EModalContainerDto` |
| HTTP Client | `*Client` interface | `EModalClient` |
| Adapter | `*Adapter` class | `KeycloakAuthAdapter` |
| Filter | `*Filter` extending `OncePerRequestFilter` | `CorrelationIdFilter` |
| Interceptor | `*Interceptor` implementing `ClientHttpRequestInterceptor` | `TokenPropagationInterceptor` |
| Config | `*Config` or `*Properties` | `HttpClientConfig`, `BackendProperties` |

## Self-Documenting Code

- Use **intention-revealing names** â€” `searchContainersByBackend` not `search`
- Prefer clarity over brevity
- Comments explain **why**, not **what**
- Extract complex conditions into named booleans or methods

```java
// BAD
if (r.isSuccess() && r.value() != null && !r.value().isEmpty()) { }

// GOOD
var hasResults = result.isSuccess() && !result.getOrElse(List.of()).isEmpty();
if (hasResults) { }
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- âŒ God classes with too many responsibilities
- âŒ Controllers depending on Handlers directly (use Dispatcher)
- âŒ Controllers depending on Ports or Clients
- âŒ Premature optimization
- âŒ Over-engineering for hypothetical requirements
- âŒ Catching generic `Exception` without proper handling
- âŒ Magic numbers and hardcoded strings
- âŒ Circular dependencies between features
- âŒ Nested record definitions (records must be top-level)
- âŒ Classes directly in feature root (must be in flow sub-packages)

## Modern Java Practices

### Use Optional for Nullable Returns

```java
// In handlers - use Result pattern instead
public Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>> handle(SearchContainersQuery query) {
    // ...
    return inventory.isEmpty() 
        ? Result.failure(DomainErrors.CONTAINER_NOT_FOUND)
        : Result.success(results);
}
```

### Use Stream API

```java
var sanitizedIds = InputSanitizer.sanitizeContainerNumbers(request.containerIds());

var results = inventory.stream()
    .map(item -> ContainerSearchResult.from(item, feeDetails))
    .toList();
```

### Use var for Local Variables

```java
var query = SearchContainersQuery.fromCode(backend, containerNumber, tradeTypeCode);
var results = dispatcher.dispatch(query)
    .getOrThrow(error -> new DomainErrorException(error, mapErrorToHttpStatus(error)));
```

## Virtual Threads

Virtual threads are enabled for optimal blocking I/O performance:

```yaml
spring:
  threads:
    virtual:
      enabled: true
```

### Parallel Operations with Virtual Threads

```java
// Execute searches in parallel - virtual threads handle blocking efficiently
var futures = query.containerIds().stream()
    .map(containerId -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
        () -> searchSingle(containerId, query.backend(), query.tradeType())
    ))
    .toList();

CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();

var searchResults = futures.stream()
    .map(CompletableFuture::join)
    .toList();
```

**Guidelines:**
- Virtual threads are suitable for I/O-bound operations (HTTP calls to backends)
- Blocking operations are fine â€” virtual threads handle them efficiently
- Use `CompletableFuture` for parallel aggregation

## Lombok Usage

### Always Use

| Annotation | Use Case |
|------------|----------|
| `@Slf4j` | Logging - creates `log` field |
| `@RequiredArgsConstructor` | Simple DI constructor for final fields |
| `@Getter` | Exception classes, enums with fields |
| `@ToString(callSuper = true)` | Exception toString |

### When NOT to Use `@RequiredArgsConstructor`

1. **Constructor has `@Value` annotations**
2. **Constructor transforms injected dependencies** (e.g., List to Map)
3. **Constructor extracts values from nested configuration**

```java
// Manual constructor required for transformation
@Slf4j
@Service
public class SearchContainersQueryHandler {
    
    private final Map<ExternalApiProvider, ContainerSearchStrategy> strategies;
    
    public SearchContainersQueryHandler(List<ContainerSearchStrategy> strategyList) {
        this.strategies = strategyList.stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(ContainerSearchStrategy::getProvider, Function.identity()));
    }
}
```

### Never Use for DTOs

```java
// GOOD - Use Java records
public record ContainerSearchResponse(List<ContainerSearchResultItemResponse> results, int count) {}

// BAD - Don't use Lombok for DTOs
@Data  // Never use this for DTOs
public class ContainerSearchResponse { ... }
```

## Boy Scout Rule

> "Always leave the code better than you found it."

- Fix small issues as you encounter them
- Remove dead code and unused imports
- Run `mvn spotless:apply` before committing

